+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,13 +9,33 @@ persistence is an in-memory repository behind a small interface.
   append-only `Ledger`; never stored. Only receipts, adjustments (counts,
   write-offs) and shipments write to the ledger.
 - **Allocated** — units promised to `PLACED` orders that have not shipped yet.
-- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated`, floored at zero. This is what new
-  orders may take.
+- **Held** — units held by `ACTIVE` reservations whose `expires_at` has not
+  been reached.
+- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated - held`, floored at zero. This is what
+  new orders and reservations may take.
 
 Order lifecycle: `place_order` (allocates, all lines or nothing) →
 `ship_order` (writes `SHIPMENT` ledger entries) or `cancel_order` (releases
 the allocation).
 
+Reservation lifecycle (checkout holds stock before payment):
+
+- `reserve(warehouse, items, idempotency_key)` holds, per line, what is
+  available now up to the quantity asked; lines with nothing available are
+  left out. If nothing can be held it raises `InsufficientStock`. Holds last
+  `reservation_ttl` (default 20 minutes, constructor argument).
+- Same idempotency key + same request returns the original reservation in its
+  current state; same key + different request raises `IdempotencyConflict`.
+- `confirm_reservation` turns an `ACTIVE` hold into a `PLACED` order for
+  exactly the held units (available does not change). Confirming again returns
+  the same order, at any time. Expired → `ReservationExpired`; released →
+  `InvalidReservationState`.
+- `release_reservation` frees the hold. Releasing a released or expired hold
+  is a no-op; a confirmed one raises `InvalidReservationState` (cancel the
+  order instead).
+- Expiry is lazy: a hold stops counting at `expires_at` (`now >= expires_at`)
+  and reads as `EXPIRED` from then on. There is no sweep job.
+
 ## Conventions
 
 - All time comes from an injected `Clock` (`FixedClock` in tests). Never call
